# Claritty Agentic App — Cursor / AI editor rules

A **self-hostable** agentic web app: FastAPI backend + Vite/React frontend +
Postgres. You host it yourself (Docker or your own infra). It depends on Claritty
for exactly two things:

1. **AI** — call models ONLY through the Claritty SDK's LLM proxy
   (`from claritty_sdk.llm import get_llm_client`). NEVER use a raw provider SDK
   or an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. The proxy is reached via `CLARITTY_PLATFORM_URL` +
   `CLARITTY_AUTH_TOKEN` (set in `.env`); with neither set, the SDK calls each
   agent's `fallback(ctx)` method (a deterministic, no-AI result) so the app still
   runs locally. Give every agent that needs the model a `fallback(ctx)`.
2. **Widget UI** — build dashboard widgets with the Claritty UI kit
   `@clarittyai/widget-toolkit` (`WidgetContainer`, `WidgetButton`, `WidgetBadge`).

## Required env vars (don't delete these — the app needs them)
- `DATABASE_URL` — Postgres connection (required).
- `CLARITTY_PLATFORM_URL` + `CLARITTY_AUTH_TOKEN` — the LLM proxy (required for
  real AI; optional locally — agents degrade via `fallback(ctx)`).

## Structure
- `backend/models.py` — SQLAlchemy models. **Every user-data model has a
  `user_id` column and EVERY query filters by it** (multi-tenancy).
- `backend/routes/app.py` — the app's HTTP API (`@router.get/post(...)`). Read the
  caller from the **`X-User-ID`** header (`_resolve_user`) — there is NO
  `CLARITY_WORKSPACE_ID`.
- `intelligence.yaml` — the v2 MANIFEST: declares agents, tools, workflows, triggers (schema lives
  here). The SDK runs THIS. Agents are a system prompt (`promptFile` → zero-Python, or a
  `@agent(id)` + `system_prompt` class — NEVER `def execute()`/`AgentResult`). Workflows +
  triggers are YAML. Do NOT create `backend/workflows/*.py` or `backend/triggers/*.py` — the
  runtime ignores them and rejects v1 `execute()` at boot.
- `backend/custom/agents/<id>/prompt.md` — a custom agent's instructions (prose).
  `backend/custom/tools/<id>/impl.py` — `@tool(id)` `def run(input, ctx)`; agents reach
  external services only through tools via `ctx.integration(...)`.
- `frontend/src/components/Widget.tsx` — the dashboard widget (uses the UI kit).
- `frontend/src/pages/*` + `frontend/src/components/ui/*` — full-app screens.
  `components/ui/` has app primitives (Button/Input/Card/Dialog/Table/...).
- Schema changes go through **Alembic** migrations (see below), never ad-hoc.

## Make it YOUR app — don't ship the template look (see IDENTITY.md)
This is a TEMPLATE. Replacing backend logic is not enough — you MUST give the app
its own identity, or it looks exactly like the seed. An identity gate
(`scripts/check-not-template.mjs`, run as a Stop hook / `npm run check:identity` /
CI) blocks "done" until you do. First: `rm .claritty-seed-pristine`.
- Fill `frontend/src/theme.css` with YOUR palette + font — set `--brand-accent`,
  `--brand-accent-600`, `--brand-primary`, `--brand-font`. Token NAMES are fixed
  (the kit reads them); you change their VALUES. This is the biggest lever.
- Replace `frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.tsx` (it's a template showcase) with your
  real landing page; remove `AgentGraph`/`HowItWorks`/`WidgetGallery`.
- Swap `/claritty-logo.png` in `frontend/src/components/Layout.tsx` for your mark;
  reskin `components/ui/*`; set real `appName`/`appDescription` in `lib/app-meta.ts`.
- Delete the seed `example_agent`/`example_workflow`/`example_trigger`; build your own.
KEEP the contract: endpoints, SDK decorators, widget sizes, infra, multi-tenancy,
and the CSS token NAMES.

## Widgets — Apple HIG, THREE sizes (canonical: `frontend/src/lib/widget-sizes.ts`)
- small **170×170**, medium **360×170**, large **360×360**.
- Build with the kit: `<WidgetContainer size={size}>…</WidgetContainer>` +
  `WidgetButton` / `WidgetBadge`. Don't hand-roll the card or set
  width/height/rounded/overflow yourself — the kit does it.
- Branch on the `size` prop into three distinct layouts. No responsive prefixes
  (`sm:`/`md:`), no `@media`, no `window.innerWidth` — widgets are fixed-size.
- The widget runs in an iframe sized EXACTLY to it: **no box-shadow**, and the host
  (`WidgetPage.tsx`) renders the bare widget with **no bg/padding/margin** (transparent
  `widget-host` body — see index.css). See WIDGETS.md → "Exact-size iframe".

## Make it actually work (not just compile — see CLAUDE.md "Build patterns" + INTEGRATIONS.md)
- If the app acts on an external service (post/send/charge/sync…), SHIP a way to connect it: a
  Connect page + per-user creds in `UserIntegration` + a pluggable action that SIMULATES until
  connected. Infer the obvious platform if the user didn't name one, and confirm. (INTEGRATIONS.md)
- If a human should approve before acting: model `draft → approved → published|failed` + an
  `/approve` endpoint that performs the action + a widget approve quick-action.
- No local scheduler: `SCHEDULE_*` triggers fire only on the platform. Locally run workflows on
  demand (`POST /api/workflows/{id}/execute`); the widget updates after a run.
- App-specific secrets in `.env` reach the backend (compose loads `env_file: .env`).

## Dev workflow (self-hosted)
- `docker compose up --build` → app on http://localhost:3200 (nginx → FastAPI).
- DB schema: `alembic -c backend/alembic.ini revision --autogenerate -m "..."`
  then `alembic -c backend/alembic.ini upgrade head` (the app also runs
  `upgrade head` on startup).
- Frontend tests: `npm run test:widgets`.

## DON'T
- ❌ Don't add provider API keys (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`) or import
  `anthropic`/`openai` directly — use `get_llm_client`.
- ❌ Don't implement 2 widget sizes or 190×190/400×190 — it's 3 sizes (170/360).
- ❌ Don't reference `CLARITY_WORKSPACE_ID` — tenancy is the `X-User-ID` header.
- ❌ Don't forget `.filter(Model.user_id == user_id)` on user-data queries.
- ❌ Don't `create_all` new columns — write an Alembic migration.
- ❌ Don't leave `theme.css` empty, the template `Dashboard.tsx`, the Claritty logo,
  `appName='Claritty Template'`, or the example agents — the identity gate fails.
- ❌ Don't rename the CSS token variables (`--brand-accent`, `--accent`, …) — change
  their values in `theme.css`, not their names.
